# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build
/storage/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# Office lock files. `docs/` holds committed .xlsx fixtures, and opening one leaves a
# `~$name.xlsx` beside it that looks like a new file to commit.
~$*

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files
#
# Every `*.example` profile is committed on purpose: they are the documentation of what
# each environment does, and a profile nobody can read is a profile nobody follows.
#
# The exception was named file by file, so `.env.local.example` and `.env.test.example`
# were silently ignored the moment they were added — the pattern only knew about the two
# that existed when it was written. A file that is never committed and never complained
# about is the worst way to lose one.
.env*
!.env*.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
